#name "Chondathan Levy"
#descr "The Chondathans were the dominant human culture-group in the interior of Faerûn. Their lineage could be traced back to the natives of the Vilhon Reach and the rise of the ancient empire of Jhaamdath, founded in -5750 DR. Jhaamdath eventually stretched from the Dragon Coast in the west to Unther in the east. It  included the lands of modern Impiltur and Vaasa north of the Sea of Fallen Stars and stretched southwards deep into the Shaar. It competed for centuries with Calimshan for the Arnaden, with the Mulan and Rashemi for the lands that now comprise Mulhorand, Thay and Narfell, and with the Netherese for what is today the Dalelands and Western Heartlands. Jaamdath was destroyed by a great tidal wave wrought by the Elven High Mages of Nikerymath and Aryselmalyr in -255 DR, in response to centuries of invasion and broken promises. 

The collapse of Jhaamdath forever changed the Heartlands and its people. The great flood drastically altered the landscape and connected the Inner Sea by winding waterways to the Shining Sea, forming the Vilhon Reach. The survivors of Jhaamdath spread in all directions, eventually growing in number and founded new cities throughout Faerûn, and their name altered over time into Chondath. They are a hardy, risk-taking folk, renowned as shrewd merchants and prizing their freedom from oppression above all else.  

Chondathan Levies are expected to bring their own equipment to the fight. They are accustomed to danger and can be rapidly recruited in times of need."
