#descr "Native human tribes south of the Marching Mountains were absorbed into the lower class of the nation of Coramshan, in the region that would later become Calimshan, around -6100 DR. The tribes farther north in what is now western Tethyr had been under the rule of High Shanatar during much of this time, but were enslaved by the Calishites by -2600 DR when High Shanatar fell. -339 DR saw the fall of the Netheril and the subsequent diaspora of the lower classes of the Netherese further added to this great mixing of western Faerûnian cultures. A series of revolts that followed along the sword and shining coasts, bringing the Illuskan culture into the melting pot and the restulting societies that emerged are now known collectively as the Tethyrians.  

