#selectmonster 3509 -- Wizard's Apprentice
#descr "Students coming to Shadowdale to learn magic were often shocked at the sight of Elminster's tower. The abode of perhaps the most famous spellcaster throughout Faerûn kept a rather plain and ramshackle keep for such a great wizard. Found just north of the village of Shadowdale, it sat in the shadow of the Old Skull Tor, a large and bare hill north of the village. Near a small pond, only three stories tall and with kudzu vines covering nearly the whole of it, was the tower of the greatest wizard who ever lived. Lean-tos and shacks had been added to the exterior over the centuries - all to accommodate Elminster's growing collection of items both magical and mundane. 

The front of the tower was adorned with a simple wooden door and the inside was just as plain. A small kitchen and office on the first floor, a spiral stair to Elminster's personal quarters on the second, and an even smaller guest room on the third floor which was sometimes used to house Elminster's lone scribe and personal assistant.

Instead, it was at the Twisted Tower where most students found themselves, walking the halls between library, scriptorium, and the mess hall, lost in books and dreams."  
#clearspec
#end





